===========================================
🚀 LSM TREE — ULTRA DEEP DIVE (FAANG LEVEL)
===========================================

🔥 FIRST PRINCIPLE (WHY LSM TREE EXISTS?)
-----------------------------------------
👉 Disk has 2 types of operations:

1) Random Write ❌ (VERY SLOW)
2) Sequential Write ✅ (VERY FAST)

👉 B-Tree problem:
   - Random disk updates (node splits, rebalancing)
   - Write becomes expensive 😵

💡 LSM IDEA:
👉 "Never update in place"
👉 "Always append"

➡️ Convert random writes → sequential writes

===========================================
🧠 CORE INTUITION (MENTAL MODEL)
-------------------------------------------
Soch tu notes likh raha hai 📓:

❌ B-Tree:
   Har baar purane page edit karta hai

✅ LSM Tree:
   Naya page likh deta hai
   Baad me clean/merge karta hai

👉 Write fast, clean later


===========================================
🏗️ COMPONENTS (BUILDING BLOCKS)
===========================================

1️⃣ WAL (Write Ahead Log)
---------------------------------
👉 Disk pe append-only log

Example:
[PUT A=1]
[PUT B=2]

✔️ Crash recovery
✔️ Durability guarantee

---------------------------------

2️⃣ MEMTABLE (IN MEMORY)
---------------------------------
👉 Sorted structure (Red-Black / AVL)

Example:
A=1, B=2, C=3 (sorted)

✔️ Fast writes (RAM)
✔️ Maintains order

---------------------------------

3️⃣ SSTABLE (ON DISK)
---------------------------------
👉 Sorted String Table

🔥 KEY PROPERTIES:
✔️ Sorted
✔️ Immutable (VERY IMPORTANT)
✔️ Stored on disk

Example:
File1: A=1, B=2
File2: B=3, D=4

---------------------------------

===========================================
✍️ WRITE PATH (STEP BY STEP)
===========================================

Step 1:
👉 Write to WAL (disk)

Step 2:
👉 Insert into MemTable (RAM)

Step 3:
👉 MemTable FULL?

   YES →
   Flush to disk → Create SSTable

   NO →
   Continue writing

---------------------------------

🔥 KEY OBSERVATION:
👉 Disk write = sequential only
👉 Hence VERY FAST 🚀


===========================================
📖 READ PATH (VERY IMPORTANT)
===========================================

👉 Search order:

1) MemTable
2) Newest SSTable
3) Older SSTables...

---------------------------------

⚠️ PROBLEM:
👉 Same key multiple places ho sakta hai

Example:
MemTable: B=5
SST2:     B=3
SST1:     B=2

👉 Correct answer = latest (B=5)

---------------------------------

⚠️ READ COST:
👉 Multiple files check karne padte hain 😵


===========================================
🗑️ DELETE OPERATION (TOMBSTONE)
===========================================

🔥 BIG QUESTION:
👉 "Agar SSTable immutable hai, toh delete kaise?"

💡 ANSWER:
👉 We DON'T delete
👉 We MARK as deleted

---------------------------------

🧠 WHAT IS TOMBSTONE?
---------------------------------
👉 Special marker indicating:
   "This key is deleted"

---------------------------------

Example:

Initial:
SST1: A=1, B=2

Delete B:

MemTable:
B = TOMBSTONE ❌

Flush → SST2:
B = TOMBSTONE

---------------------------------

📖 READ BEHAVIOR:
---------------------------------
👉 If tombstone found → key treated as deleted

---------------------------------

🔥 WHY TOMBSTONE?
---------------------------------
👉 Immutable files → can't remove entry
👉 So we override with delete marker

---------------------------------

⚠️ PROBLEM:
---------------------------------
👉 Data still exists in old SSTables
👉 Disk waste

---------------------------------

💡 SOLUTION:
👉 COMPACTION (later remove permanently)


===========================================
⚠️ MAJOR PROBLEMS IN LSM TREE
===========================================

1) MANY SSTABLES
   👉 Too many files → slow reads

2) DUPLICATE KEYS
   👉 Same key multiple versions

3) TOMBSTONES
   👉 Deleted data still taking space

4) READ AMPLIFICATION
   👉 One read → many disk reads 😵


===========================================
💡 OPTIMIZATIONS (VERY IMPORTANT)
===========================================

---------------------------------
1️⃣ BLOOM FILTER 🌸
---------------------------------

🧠 INTUITION:
👉 "Avoid unnecessary disk reads"

👉 Fast probabilistic structure

---------------------------------

✔️ If says "NOT PRESENT" → 100% true
❌ If says "PRESENT" → maybe

---------------------------------

Example:
Search key=Z

Bloom filter:
→ "Not present"

👉 Skip SSTable entirely 🚀

---------------------------------

2️⃣ SPARSE INDEX
---------------------------------

🧠 INTUITION:
👉 Don't store full index (too big)

👉 Store checkpoints

---------------------------------

Example:
Store:
A → offset 0
M → offset 500
Z → offset 1000

👉 Binary search → jump → scan small range

---------------------------------

3️⃣ COMPACTION (MOST IMPORTANT)
---------------------------------

🧠 INTUITION:
👉 "Clean garbage + merge data"

---------------------------------

Example:

Before:
SST1: A=1, B=2
SST2: B=3, C=4
SST3: B=TOMBSTONE

---------------------------------

After compaction:
👉 Remove old versions
👉 Apply latest updates

Result:
A=1, C=4

(B removed completely)

---------------------------------

🔥 TYPES OF COMPACTION:
---------------------------------

1) Size-tiered
   👉 Merge similar size files

2) Leveled compaction
   👉 Organized in levels (L1, L2...)

---------------------------------

⚠️ TRADEOFF:
---------------------------------
✔️ Clean data
❌ Background CPU + IO cost


===========================================
📊 AMPLIFICATION CONCEPTS (INTERVIEW GOLD)
===========================================

1️⃣ WRITE AMPLIFICATION
---------------------------------
👉 One write → multiple disk writes

Reason:
Compaction

---------------------------------

2️⃣ READ AMPLIFICATION
---------------------------------
👉 One read → multiple SSTable reads

---------------------------------

3️⃣ SPACE AMPLIFICATION
---------------------------------
👉 Extra disk usage due to:
   - duplicates
   - tombstones

---------------------------------


===========================================
⚔️ LSM vs B-TREE (DEEP INSIGHT)
===========================================

LSM:
👉 Write optimized
👉 Sequential writes
👉 Background cleanup

B-Tree:
👉 Read optimized
👉 Random writes
👉 Immediate consistency

---------------------------------

🔥 KEY INTERVIEW LINE:
---------------------------------
👉 LSM delays work (lazy cleanup)
👉 B-Tree does work immediately


